<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <p><strong>Step 11:</strong> Continue the assembly of extension plenums following the same procedure. At the end of the final extension plenum, the end duct assembly must be installed.</p>
            <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">
                <img src="placeholder_image.png" alt="Figure 23" style="max-width: 100%;">
                <div class="figure-caption">Figure 23. Assembly of end duct to the last segment of the plenum.</div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If the customer chooses to install their own version of end duct segment, the duct must allow a minimum open exhaust area of <span data-field="area_value">{{ area_value }}</span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="text-align: center;">Turned Extension Plenum Installation Guide (Front/Rear)</h3>
            <p>At the installation site, remove all separately packaged components shipped inside the Limitamp AR unit. Find the Turned Plenum, and mounting hardware and place them in the work area.</p>
            <p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Remove top cover plate on existing extension plenum for assembly. Apply sealer around perimeter of existing extension plenum side flanges, where turned plenum (Front/Rear) will be attached.</p>
            <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 20px;">
                <img src="placeholder_image.png" alt="Figure 25" style="max-width: 100%;">
                <div class="figure-caption">Figure 25. Apply sealer around perimeter of plenum.</div>
            </div>
            <p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Install 3/8" hardware to fasten the turned plenum (Front/Rear) to the extension plenum.</p>
